    INSERT INTO mcqs (topic_id, question, options, correct_index, explanation) VALUES
    (v_topic_id, 'A 73-year-old female named Florence has just been diagnosed with mild Alzheimer''s disease. Her grandson asks the clinician, ''What should we plan for over the next few years?'' Which of the following represents the most appropriate and comprehensive response regarding the caregiver trajectory in Alzheimer''s disease?', '["Tell the grandson that home care for Alzheimer''s is unsustainable beyond 6 months and immediate nursing home placement is the clinically recommended option", "Provide anticipatory guidance: caregiving demands will progressively increase as the disease advances through mild, moderate, and severe stages; early-stage planning should include legal/financial preparations (power of attorney, advance directives), identifying future care resources, caregiver support enrollment, and discussing the likely eventual need for residential care", "Focus exclusively on pharmacological management of the patient''s symptoms and defer all social planning discussions to a separate social work appointment next year", "Advise the family to purchase a long-term care insurance policy immediately, as this is the only reliable funding source for future dementia care", "Reassure the caregiver that Alzheimer''s disease has a very gradual course requiring minimal caregiving adjustments over time, and no long-term planning is necessary at this early stage"]'::jsonb, 1, '**Anticipatory guidance in dementia caregiving** is a proactive, staged planning approach recognizing that Alzheimer''s disease progresses through predictable stages with escalating care demands. Early-stage planning (FAST Stage 3–4) should address: (1) **Legal**: durable power of attorney (financial and healthcare), advance directives (POLST, living will); (2) **Financial**: benefits counseling, long-term care insurance eligibility, spend-down planning; (3) **Social/community**: enroll caregiver in support groups, identify adult day programs, respite care resources; (4) **Future care planning**: discuss realistic trajectory, identify when nursing home placement may become necessary (wandering, incontinence, behavioral disturbances). Early planning reduces crisis decision-making and caregiver burden. The geriatrician should initiate these discussions at the time of diagnosis, not after a crisis. (Ref: Hazzard''s Ch. 73; AGS Geriatrics At Your Fingertips; Current Diagnosis & Treatment: Geriatrics)'),
