tives**: in-home aides, PACE, culturally aligned day programs, community health workers from the same cultural background; (4) **Provide resources** in the family''s language; (5) **Monitor for caregiver burnout** and patient safety — without judgment. Forcing institutional placement against family values is ethically and legally inappropriate when the patient is safe. (Ref: Hazzard''s Ch. 17; AGS Geriatrics At Your Fingertips; Current Diagnosis & Treatment: Geriatrics)'),
